    "q-161129": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161129",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of $z=3{x}^{2}-y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$ What is the missing expression?",
      "worked_solution": "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=3{x}^{2}-y,\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2.\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}-y)=6x, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}-y)=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(6x)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+36{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{2+36{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\sqrt{2+36{x}^{2}}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
